  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#link-type-preload says:\r\n\r\n> If as does not represent a state, return false.\r\n\r\nI'm wondering if the word \"state\" here should actually be \"potential destination\"?  If not, maybe either \"represent\" or \"state\" should be hyperlinked to a definition?  As it is, I don't understand what this sentence means.",
